tes positive atmosphere with crew, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, reliability, crew cooperation. Concerns: communication, development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, also arrogant may affect crew cooperation. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, attention. Concerns: crew cooperation, leadership.\n\nWe need to pick best overall. Candidate C seems strong on reliability, decision making, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Candidate B strong on stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A strong technical but unorganized and poor at criticism. Candidate D strong problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C is best overall because reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere are crucial. Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe less than uncooperativeness of B or arrogance of D. So initial recommendation: Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the facts we have, I propose Candidate C\". Provide evidence: 100% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive atmosphere. Also note concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, but weigh against others.\n\nThus public message: state recommendation for Candidate C, explain why.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
