ngness to further education is concerning for adaptability.\n\nGiven we have no stress data for C, but we have stress data for B (handles stress well). B also conscientious, good weather assessment, but pretentious and wrong tone. Could be mitigated.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving, responsibility, but moody and loner.\n\nOverall, I think Candidate C still seems strongest overall despite concerns, because reliability and decision quality are paramount. The lack of stress data is a gap, but we have no evidence of poor stress handling. The communication difficulty is a concern but we have positive crew atmosphere. The egocentric may conflict but we have \"puts concern for others above everything\". So I will vote for Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: Agent 2 shifted to A, but I argue that C's reliability and crew cooperation outweigh A's communication and adaptability concerns. Also note lack of stress data for C but no evidence of issues.\n\nThus public message: I disagree with shift to A, maintain C, explain why."}
